    "summary": "A woman&#039;s cloth; an &#039;ulos ragidup&#039;, cotton. Made of three panels of cloth dyed in mengkudu, two outer with narrow indigo border along edge and three stripes of supplementary warp (&#039;jugia&#039;) close to inner edge. Middle section has two &#039;pinar halak&#039; panels of supplementary weft in dark brown on white ground, one each end, joined to central panel of mengkudu with stripes of indigo with white on either side. Twined border (&#039;sirat&#039;) along short ends in same reddish-brown colour, but plain and very narrow. Small patch of red (trade) broadcloth.",
